"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>For solid cylinder,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.887ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"18.278ex\" height=\"3.592ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1195.6 8078.9 1587.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(837.5,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-377.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1051,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(792,289) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g><rect width=\"1788.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2306.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(3362.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,584) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(793.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1844.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(792,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(500.6,-377.4) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D440\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D440\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1051,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(792,289) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g><rect width=\"2349.7\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6229.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(7285.3,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Acceleration of the solid cylinder is more than that of hollow cylinder and therefore solid cylinder will reach the bottom of the inclined plane first.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.509ex\" height=\"1.251ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -471 667 553\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2234\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2234\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Statement - 1 is False.</p>\n<p>Statement - 2 : In case of rolling, there will be no heat losses. Therefore, total mechanical energy remains conserved. The potential energy, therefore gets converted into kinetic energy. In both the cases, since the initial potential energy is same, the final kinetic energy will also be same. Therefore, statement - 2 is correct.</p>"}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"combined-translational-and-rotational-motion","type":"mcq","year":2008,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2008-paper-1-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1lfur1647","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":3,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"iit-jee-2008-paper-1-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline","permalink":"pstatement-1p-pthe-stream-of-water-flowing-at-high-jee-advanced-physics-motion-jv9gr0heljhpojn2","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p><b>STATEMENT - 1 :</b></p>\n<p>The stream of water flowing at high speed from a garden hose pipe tends to spread line a fountain when held vertically up, but tends to narrow down when held vertically down.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p><b>STATEMENT - 2 :</b></p>\n<p>In any steady flow of an incompressible fluid, the volume flow rate of the fluid remains constant.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is True; Statement - 2 is a correct explanation for Statement - 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is True; Statement - 2 is NOT a correct explanation for Statement - 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement - 1 is True, Statement - 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement - 1 is False, Statement - 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Volume flow rate (V) of an incompressible fluid in the steady flow remains constant.</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.817ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 4339 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1046.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2102.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2853.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3854,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.197ex\" height=\"1.02ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -441 529 451\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = area of cross-section and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.097ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 485 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = velocity</p>\n<p>If '<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.097ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 485 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>' decreases, '<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.023ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.197ex\" height=\"1.02ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -441 529 451\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>' increases and vice-versa.</p>\n<p>When steam of water moves up, its speed (v) decreases and therefore 'a' increases, i.e., the water spreads out like a fountain. When steam of water from hose pipe moves down, its speed increases and as a result, area of cross-section decreases.</p>\n<p>Therefore, statement - 1 is true.</p>\n<p>Statement - 2 is the correct explanation of statement - 1.</p>"}},"subject":"physics","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":200000,"topic":"fluid-flow-bernoullis-principle-and-viscosity","type":"mcq","year":2008,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2008-paper-1-offline","active":true}],"ids":["1lfuqcf1v","1lfuqm8m6","1lfuqtqwv","1lfur1647"],"title":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 1 Offline | JEE Advanced Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/pstatement-1p-pin-a-meter-bridge-experiment-null-p-jee-advanced-physics-motion-5sdsszs9tkefi8ju"}